{{!-- ApplicationV2 renders this part straight into `.window-content`, which is
itself the sheet's <form> element — hence no <form> wrapper here. --}}

  {{!-- Banner: das Band über dem Tab-Körper. Drei Bahnen: das Porträt, die
  Identität mit den Vitalwerten, und rechts die zwei Steuerpillen.

  Der Schnitt ist der zwischen "was ist an dieser Figur wahr" und "was ist
  gerade wahr" — mit einer bewussten Ausnahme, die der Entwurf trifft: Malus,
  Schadensleisten und die Zustandszeile stehen in der Identitätsbahn statt in
  der Metabahn, weil der Malus in derselben Grundlinie wie der Name gelesen
  wird, die Leisten unter ihm hängen und die Zustände aus ihnen folgen. Die
  rechte Bahn führt dafür nur noch, was gewählt wird: Haltung und Edge.

  Was nicht mehr hier steht: 6. Sinn und Initiative stehen als abgeleitete Werte
  unter der Attributsmatrix im Grundlagen-Tab, die Bewegung unter der getragenen
  Ausrüstung; Raster,
  Stepper, Löschen-Aktion und das Edge-Zahlenfeld liegen hinter je einem Klick
  in ihrem Panel. Im Band würfelt nichts mehr.

  Das Porträt hängt bewusst über die Unterkante des Bandes; `.sheet-body`
  reserviert die Höhe, die es braucht. --}}
  <header class="sheet-banner">

    {{!-- One decorative copy forms the banner image and fades into parchment
    behind the identity. The real portrait below remains the only semantic
    image and edit target. --}}
    <div class="banner-backdrop" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="banner-backdrop-image" src="{{actor.img}}" alt="" />
    </div>

    {{!-- The portrait is only the character image. Owners get a quiet edit
    affordance; read-only viewers get an ordinary image with no dead action.
    With both rollables gone from the band it is the only element left here
    that `_makeKeyboardAccessible()` has to promote. --}}
    <div class="banner-portrait{{#if editable}} is-editable{{/if}}">
      <img class="profile-img" src="{{actor.img}}" alt="{{actor.name}}" height="170" width="170"
        {{#if editable}}data-edit="img" data-action="editImage" aria-label="{{localize 'TNO.PortraitEdit'}}" title="{{localize 'TNO.PortraitEdit'}}"{{else}}title="{{actor.name}}"{{/if}} />
      {{#if editable}}
      <span class="portrait-edit-hint" aria-hidden="true">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-pen"></i>
        <span>{{localize "TNO.PortraitEdit"}}</span>
      </span>
      {{/if}}
    </div>

    {{!-- Name and malus on one baseline, then the subtitle the player owns: a
    free-text profession or role with the total XP spent across attributes and
    skills at the end of that same line, then the two damage tracks.

    `system.role` is flavour text and nothing else. The system has no concept of
    a class or profession — no roll, derived value, or gate reads this field, and
    none should start to: it is the player's space to say who their character is.
    Anything that ought to have mechanical weight belongs in skills or an item.

    The XP beside it is a computed read-out, so it sits outside the input; the
    field hugs its own text (see `field-sizing` in _forms.scss) so the figure
    trails the role rather than floating at the far side of the lane. XP stays
    in the band rather than leaving with the other properties because it is part
    of this sentence and costs no lane of its own. --}}
    <div class="banner-identity">

      <div class="banner-headline">
        <h1 class="charname"><input name="name" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" placeholder="Name"/></h1>
        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-malus.hbs"}}
      </div>

      <div class="banner-subtitle">
        <input class="banner-role" name="system.role" type="text" value="{{system.role}}"
               placeholder="{{localize 'TNO.RolePlaceholder'}}" title="{{localize 'TNO.RoleHint'}}" />
        {{!-- Spent over acquired, dimming the total: the left figure is what has
        been committed to ranks, the right what the character has earned all
        told. They close the gap only when nothing is left banked. --}}
        <span class="banner-xp tno-tooltip-hint"
              data-tooltip-html='<dl class="tno-tooltip">
<div class="tno-tooltip-row"><dt>{{localize "TNO.UnitXp"}} <span class="tno-tooltip-value">{{totalXpSpent}}/{{totalXpAcquired}}</span></dt><dd>{{localize "TNO.XpTotalAllHint" spent=totalXpSpent acquired=totalXpAcquired unspent=totalXpUnspent}}</dd></div>
</dl>'
              data-tooltip-direction='DOWN'>{{totalXpSpent}}<span class="banner-xp-total">/{{totalXpAcquired}}</span> {{localize "TNO.UnitXp"}}</span>
      </div>

      {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-damage.hbs"}}

      {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-status.hbs"}}

    </div>

    {{!-- Die Metabahn: zwei Pillen, beide Bedienelemente, beide auf dieselbe
    Frage — was wähle ich gerade. Die Haltung führt sie an, weil sie im Kampf am
    häufigsten geändert wird und allein entscheidet, ob es überhaupt eine
    Verteidigung gibt. Die von ihr freigeschalteten Handlungen liegen an ihren
    eigenen Spielflächen: Ausweichen an der Papierpuppe, Parade an der Waffe.

    Not `disabled` when read-only: a disabled button fires no pointer events,
    and the Haltung's tooltip is exactly what a player reading someone else's
    sheet is after. The click is gated on `editable` in the sheet. --}}
    <div class="banner-state">

      <button type="button" class="banner-chip chip-stance{{#unless editable}} disabled{{/unless}}"
              aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false"
              {{#unless editable}}aria-disabled="true"{{/unless}}
              data-tooltip-html='<dl class="tno-tooltip">
<div class="tno-tooltip-row"><dt>{{localize "TNO.Combat.StanceLabel"}}</dt><dd>{{localize "TNO.Combat.StanceHint"}}</dd></div>
</dl>'
              data-tooltip-direction='DOWN'>
        <span class="chip-label">{{localize "TNO.Combat.StanceLabel"}}</span>
        <span class="chip-stance-name">
          <i class="fa-solid {{stance.icon}} chip-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>{{stance.label}}</span>
        </span>
        <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down chip-stance-caret" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </button>

      {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-edge.hbs"}}

    </div>

  </header>

  {{!-- Sheet Body --}}
  <section class="sheet-body">

    {{!-- Basics Tab, as two full-width rows rather than a left/right split.
    Top: the attribute matrix, what is on the body, and the zero-slot pocket.
    Bottom: the skill list and the slot raster — the two long lists, each of
    which wants width more than the blocks above them do.

    Every boundary between two columns is a draggable handle, and each row keeps
    its own set of shares (`basicsLayout`, client-scoped): a handle only ever
    redistributes the pair it sits between, so a row of three columns has two
    independent boundaries rather than one split running the sheet's height. --}}
    <div class="tab basics {{tabs.basics.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="basics">
      <div class="basics-rows">

      <div class="basics-row" data-split-row="top">

      <section class="basics-cell cell-attributes flexcol">

        {{!-- Primary attributes, laid out as a heatmap: one column per category
        (körperlich/sozial/geistig) and one row per attribute pairing,
        mirroring the "Attribute" table in the rulebook. Cell and sum-badge
        backgrounds are color-graded relative to the character's own values,
        ported from the "Attribut-Heatmap" prototype. --}}
        <div class="basics-section-header attributes-header flexrow">
          <h3 class="basics-section-title attributes-title">{{localize "TNO.AttributesTitle"}} <span class="xp-badge"
              data-tooltip-html='<dl class="tno-tooltip"><div class="tno-tooltip-row"><dd>{{localize "TNO.XpTotalAttributesHint"}}</dd></div></dl>'
              data-tooltip-direction='DOWN'>{{attributeGrid.totalValue}} {{localize "TNO.UnitPoints"}} · {{attributeGrid.totalXp}} {{localize "TNO.UnitXp"}}</span></h3>
          {{#if isGM}}
          <a class="heatmap-lab-btn" title="{{localize 'TNO.Settings.HeatmapPreset.BtnHint'}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-palette"></i></a>
          {{/if}}
        </div>
        <div class="attributes-card">
        <table class="attribute-table heatmap">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="attribute-corner"></th>
              {{#each attributeGrid.colHeaders as |col|}}
              <th>
                <span class="heatmap-col-label">{{col.label}}</span>
              </th>
              {{/each}}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {{#each attributeGrid.rows as |row|}}
            <tr>
              <th class="heatmap-row-header">
                <span class="heatmap-row-label">{{row.label}}</span>
              </th>
              {{#each row.cells as |cell|}}
              <td class="heatmap-cell{{#if cell.isPeak}} heatmap-peak{{/if}}" style="background:{{cell.cellBg}}; color:{{cell.textColor}}; border-color:{{cell.tileBorder}};" title="{{cell.hint}}">
                {{!-- Name first and full-width, value demoted to a chip in the
                top-right corner: the twelve tiles are scanned by name, and the
                badge keeps the number legible without a 18px numeral fighting
                the graded fill for the tile. --}}
                <div class="heatmap-cell-top">
                  <span class="heatmap-cell-name">{{cell.label}}</span>
                  <strong class="heatmap-value" style="background:{{cell.badgeBg}};">{{cell.value}}</strong>
                </div>
                <a class="heatmap-xp-bar{{#if cell.xpReady}} ready{{/if}}" data-key="{{cell.key}}" style="background:{{cell.xpBarTrack}};" title="{{#if cell.xpAtMax}}{{localize 'TNO.XpMaxBadge'}}{{else}}{{cell.xp}}/{{cell.xpCost}} xp{{/if}} — {{localize 'TNO.AttributeAdvanceHint'}}">
                  <span class="heatmap-xp-bar-fill" style="width:{{cell.xpPercent}}%; background:{{cell.xpBarFill}};"></span>
                </a>
              </td>
              {{/each}}
            </tr>
            {{/each}}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>

        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-derived.hbs"}}

      </section>

      <div class="basics-splitter" role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical" tabindex="0"
           title="{{localize 'TNO.BasicsSplitterHint'}}"></div>

      {{!-- What the character is wearing right now: the armour paper doll and
      its four zone read-outs. The Inventar tab keeps the flat administrative
      list — creating, editing and deleting items — but this answers "what am I
      wearing?", which is a question asked mid-roll, so it sits beside the
      attributes rather than a tab away. --}}
      <section class="basics-cell cell-gear flexcol">
        <div class="basics-section-header gear-header flexrow">
          <h3 class="basics-section-title cell-title">{{localize "TNO.Armor.WornTitle"}}</h3>
        </div>
        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-paperdoll.hbs"}}
        {{!-- Die Bewegung schließt diese Spalte ab: die Stufe, die die Last
        wegnimmt, steht damit unter der Summe der Stärkevoraussetzung, die sie
        wegnimmt. --}}
        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-movement.hbs"}}
      </section>

      <div class="basics-splitter" role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical" tabindex="0"
           title="{{localize 'TNO.BasicsSplitterHint'}}"></div>

      {{!-- Papers and other zero-slot gear remain ordinary draggable items.
      Money is separate actor state and follows Kleinkram as the quieter,
      secondary bookkeeping surface in the same column. --}}
      <section class="basics-cell cell-loose flexcol">
        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-trinkets.hbs"}}
        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-money-wallet.hbs"}}
      </section>

      </div>

      <div class="basics-row" data-split-row="bottom">

      <section class="basics-cell cell-skills flexcol">

        {{!-- Skills, grouped by category. Each skill rolls with its linked
        attribute; the rank is added as the roll dialog's starting bonus. --}}
        <div class="basics-section-header skills-header flexrow">
          <h3 class="basics-section-title skills-title">{{localize "TNO.SkillsTitle"}} <span class="xp-badge"
              data-tooltip-html='<dl class="tno-tooltip"><div class="tno-tooltip-row"><dd>{{localize "TNO.XpTotalSkillsHint"}}</dd></div></dl>'
              data-tooltip-direction='DOWN'>{{skillRankTotal}} {{localize "TNO.UnitPoints"}} · {{skillXpTotal}} {{localize "TNO.UnitXp"}}</span></h3>
          <input type="text" class="skill-search-input" value="{{skillSearch}}" placeholder="{{localize 'TNO.SkillSearchPlaceholder'}}" title="{{localize 'TNO.SkillSearchHint'}}" />
          <div class="skill-filter-group">
            <a class="skill-filter-btn {{#ifEquals skillFilter 'trained'}}active{{/ifEquals}}" data-filter="trained" title="{{localize 'TNO.SkillFilterTrainedHint'}}">{{localize "TNO.SkillFilterTrained"}}</a>
            <a class="skill-filter-btn {{#ifEquals skillFilter 'starter'}}active{{/ifEquals}}" data-filter="starter" title="{{localize 'TNO.SkillFilterStarterHint'}}">{{localize "TNO.SkillFilterStarter"}}</a>
            <a class="skill-filter-btn {{#ifEquals skillFilter 'all'}}active{{/ifEquals}}" data-filter="all" title="{{localize 'TNO.SkillFilterAllHint'}}">{{localize "TNO.SkillFilterAll"}}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        {{!-- The inner .skill-groups is a balanced CSS multi-column flow whose
        height is content-driven inside the skills column's bounded scroll
        region. --}}
        <div class="skill-groups-scroll">
        <div class="skill-groups">
          {{#each skillGroups as |group|}}
          <div class="card basics-section-card skill-group">
            <h4 class="skill-group-title">
              <span class="skill-group-name">{{group.label}}</span>
              <span class="xp-badge">{{group.totalRank}}pt | {{group.totalXp}}xp</span>
              {{#if @root.editable}}
              <a class="skill-create-button" data-category="{{group.key}}" title="{{localize 'TNO.CustomSkill.Add'}}">
                <i class="fas fa-plus"></i>
              </a>
              {{/if}}
            </h4>
            {{#if group.skills.length}}
            <ul class="skill-list">
              {{#each group.skills as |skill|}}
              <li class="skill-row" data-rank="{{skill.rank}}" data-xp="{{skill.xp}}" data-starter="{{skill.starter}}" data-custom="{{skill.custom}}">
                <span class="skill-info rollable" data-roll-type="skill" data-skill="{{skill.key}}" data-ability="{{skill.attribute}}" data-label="{{skill.label}}" title="{{#if skill.custom}}{{localize 'TNO.CustomSkill.ShiftClickHint'}}{{else}}{{localize 'TNO.RollSkill'}}: {{skill.label}}{{/if}}">
                  <span class="skill-name">
                    {{!-- Own title so the full name still shows on hover even
                    when the outer .skill-info title is the shift-click hint
                    (custom skills) rather than the roll hint. --}}
                    <span class="skill-name-text" title="{{skill.label}}">{{skill.label}}</span>
                    {{#if skill.subgroupBadge}}
                    <span class="skill-subgroup-badge" title="{{skill.subgroupLabel}}">{{skill.subgroupBadge}}</span>
                    {{/if}}
                    {{#if skill.custom}}
                    <span class="skill-custom-badge" title="{{localize 'TNO.CustomSkill.BadgeHint'}}">{{localize "TNO.CustomSkill.Badge"}}</span>
                    {{/if}}
                  </span>
                  <span class="skill-level"{{#if skill.levelBg}} style="background:{{skill.levelBg}}; color:{{skill.levelColor}};"{{/if}}>{{skill.rank}}</span>
                  {{!-- XP-toward-next-rank bar, mirroring the attribute heatmap's
                  xp bar: fill/color communicate progress at a glance, exact
                  figures live in the tooltip, and clicking it opens the same
                  advance dialog as the arrow button beside it. --}}
                  <a class="skill-xp-bar{{#if skill.xpReady}} ready{{/if}}" data-skill="{{skill.key}}" title="{{#if skill.xpAtMax}}{{localize 'TNO.XpMaxBadge'}}{{else}}{{skill.xp}}/{{skill.xpCost}} xp{{/if}} — {{localize 'TNO.SkillAdvance'}}">
                    <span class="skill-xp-bar-fill" style="width:{{skill.xpPercent}}%;"></span>
                  </a>
                </span>
                <a class="skill-advance-button{{#if skill.xpReady}} ready{{/if}}" data-skill="{{skill.key}}" title="{{localize 'TNO.SkillAdvance'}}">
                  <i class="fas fa-arrow-up"></i>
                </a>
              </li>
              {{/each}}
            </ul>
            {{else}}
            <p class="skill-group-empty">{{localize "TNO.SkillCategoryEmptyHint"}}</p>
            {{/if}}
          </div>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
        </div>

      </section>

      <div class="basics-splitter" role="separator" aria-orientation="vertical" tabindex="0"
           title="{{localize 'TNO.BasicsSplitterHint'}}"></div>

      {{!-- What the character is hauling: the Trageslots budget, packed. Beside
      the skills rather than under the paper doll, because the raster and the
      skill list are the tab's two long lists and both want the width. --}}
      <section class="basics-cell cell-carry flexcol">
        {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-slot-grid.hbs"}}
      </section>

      </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    {{!-- Biography Tab --}}
    <div class="tab biography {{tabs.description.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="description">
      {{!-- Plain textarea instead of the ProseMirror editor helper: the
      editor requires an explicit click into an edit mode before typing,
      which is unnecessary friction for a simple freetext notes field. --}}
      <textarea name="system.biography" class="biography-textarea" placeholder="{{localize 'TNO.BiographyPlaceholder'}}">{{system.biography}}</textarea>
    </div>

    {{!-- Owned Items Tab --}}
    <div class="tab items {{tabs.items.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="items">
       {{> "systems/tno/templates/actor/parts/actor-items.hbs"}}
    </div>

  </section>

  {{!-- Sheet Tab Navigation, docked as a vertical icon rail along the right
  edge, mirroring the reference dnd5e sheet's tab layout. Each item also
  carries a text label, hidden by default and revealed on hover/focus (see
  _forms.scss), so the rail's purpose as tab navigation is discoverable
  without waiting on the native tooltip's delay. --}}
  <nav class="sheet-tabs tabs tabs-right" data-group="primary">
    {{!-- Tab set and default tab are declared in actor-sheet.mjs (static TABS);
    `data-action="tab"` is what hands the click to ApplicationV2#changeTab. --}}
    {{#each tabs as |tab|}}
    <a class="item {{tab.cssClass}}" data-action="tab" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}"><i class="{{tab.icon}}"></i><span class="tab-label">{{localize tab.label}}</span></a>
    {{/each}}
  </nav>
